}
`;

exports[`mapping the launch list > snapshots of a few mapped entries > minecraft-in-doom 1`] = `
{
  "input": {
    "buildsOn": {
      "license": "GPL-3.0",
      "name": "uzdoom",
      "url": "https://github.com/UZDoom/UZDoom",
    },
    "check": {
      "author": true,
      "people": {
        "count": 1,
        "human": true,
        "instructions": "play 10 minutes on the test map, digging a tunnel and walling yourself in while an imp wave attacks. post your fps and any block you could walk through or that placed on the wrong face. at least one tester must be human.",
      },
      "runs": {
        "command": "./bench.sh && ./license-scan.sh mcdoom.pk3",
        "count": 1,
        "description": "plays the bundled benchmark demo in uzdoom with freedoom2.wad and prints min and average fps",
      },
    },
    "doneWhen": "a downloadable uzdoom mod where you can dig and place blocks while imps attack, at 60 fps on the reference rig (a ryzen 5 3600 with a gtx 1660 at 1080p), using only freedoom and other open assets.",
    "kind": "shwarm",
    "slug": "minecraft-in-doom",
    "tags": [
      "weird",
      "games",
      "gzdoom",
      "uzdoom",
    ],
    "title": "minecraft in doom",
    "what": "freedoom already gives us monsters to fight and a free license. we add a world made of blocks that you can dig through and build with, running in uzdoom, the active fork of gzdoom. the hard part is holding 60 fps once thousands of blocks are on screen.

why now: uzdoom 5.0.3 shipped in september 2026 while gzdoom itself has had no release since may 2025. the closest mod, voxel violence, stalled at v0.3 in 2022; it needs doom ii and adds blocks only on top of normal maps.",
  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "field": "what",
      "kind": "changed",
      "text": "why_now appended as a last paragraph, "why now: uzdoom 5.0.3 shipped in september 2026 …"",
    },
    {
      "field": "check.runs",
      "kind": "changed",
      "text": "command split: "./bench.sh && ./license-scan.sh mcdoom.pk3", and the words in brackets went to runs.description: "plays the bundled benchmark demo in uzdoom with freedoom2.wad and prints min and average fps"",
    },
    {
      "field": "builds_on",
      "kind": "normalized",
      "text": "license "gpl" → GPL-3.0",
    },
    {
      "field": "builds_on",
      "kind": "warning",
      "text": ""gpl" names no version; assumed version 3.0",
    },
    {
      "field": "license",
      "kind": "changed",
      "text": "GPL-3.0, taken from uzdoom (builds on takes the upstream license)",
    },
    {
      "field": "builds_on",
      "kind": "dropped",
      "text": "1 more upstream only in the pinned post: https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom",
    },
    {
      "field": "pinned post",
      "kind": "changed",
      "text": "4 sources, plus the builds-on text as written",
    },
  ],
  "pinned": "where this pitch comes from:
https://github.com/UZDoom/UZDoom
https://www.gamingonlinux.com/2025/12/uzdoom-the-successor-to-gzdoom-has-a-first-proper-release-out-now
https://www.moddb.com/mods/voxel-violence
https://www.pcgamer.com/voxel-violence-mod-adds-minecraft-blocks-and-building-to-doom/

builds on: uzdoom (gpl, active gzdoom fork) https://github.com/UZDoom/UZDoom + freedoom (bsd) https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom",
}
`;

