        "count": 1,
      },
    },
    "doneWhen": "a model under 256 kb that runs on an esp32-s3 or rp2040 scores roc-auc of at least 0.93 on humbugdb test a and at least 0.80 on test b, without training on either test set, using the shared eval script.",
    "kind": "shwarm",
    "slug": "mosquito-hearing-chip",
    "tags": [
      "health",
      "tinyml",
      "audio",
      "benchmark",
    ],
    "title": "a $5 chip that hears mosquitoes",
    "what": "a mosquito's wings hum at a pitch you can pick out of a phone recording. humbugdb has 20 hours of labeled mosquito sound from 36 species, and the best model in its paper scored 0.77 roc-auc on the hard test set. beat that with a model small enough for a cheap microcontroller.

why now: tiny ml toolchains now fit audio models in a few hundred kb, and the dataset's hard test set is still a weak spot.",
  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "field": "what",
      "kind": "changed",
